    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389-a1">

                <pb facs="0587" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg493"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 307.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McKenzie to Dr. Zevallos.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1896-05-20"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">May 20, 1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: Referring to the conversation
                    between your excellency and the secretary of this legation on February 22 last,
                    in relation to the settlement of the claims of the members of the Hydrographic
                    Commission of the Amazon against Peru, in which you stated the Government of
                    Peru would pay in full satisfaction of all claims 20,000 silver soles, 10,000
                    this year and 10,000 next year, etc., I now have the pleasure of notifying your
                    excellency that I am authorized by the United States Government to accept your
                    proposition, and will come to the Peruvian foreign office at any time your
                    excellency may indicate to receive the first moiety and transmit it to the
                    Secretary of State for distribution among the claimants.</p>
                <p>Congratulating all parties concerned upon this friendly, honorable adjustment of
                    a long-standing claim,</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. A. McKenzie.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
